yaml/alias
description: A *name token - stands for the node the anchor named
- >
  An **alias** `*name` stands for the node an
  [anchor](*::language:concretes:04-yaml:01-yaml_code:00-yaml_structured:00-yaml_mapping:02-yaml_key_value_pair:01-yaml_anchor)
  `&name` named earlier - the very same node, shared, not a copy. This is YAML's sharing
  ceiling: an alias names a whole anchored node and can never reach INTO one - which is where
  yamlover's pointer paths begin:
- !!<format: text/x-yaml> |
  boss: &chief {name: Rex}
  team:
    lead: *chief
